I came out of the market.
There are heavy cloth bags in my hands.
The bags are very heavy.
It is very hot even in the morning.
I felt very tired.
I walked to the main road.
There are many autos on the road.
I went near an auto.
"I need to go to Kaloor," I told the driver.
"How many rupees will it be to Kaloor?"
I asked.
"It will be eighty rupees," the driver replied.
I agreed to that.
"Okay, let's go," I said.
First, I placed the bags in the auto.
Then I climbed in and sat in the auto.
The auto started the journey to my flat.
I felt very relieved.
